      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **H**. An absolute date refers to a specific year or range of years (e.g., 1492 CE), while a relative date places events in chronological order without exact years (e.g., \"before the war\" or \"after the eruption\"). This distinction is fundamental in fields like archaeology and history.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
