      "generated_answer": "In archaeology, **primary context** refers to an artifact or feature found in the exact position where it was originally deposited by its users, undisturbed by subsequent human or natural activity. A **cache** (Option H) is a classic example of primary context because the items remain exactly where they were intentionally placed. Other options, such as erosion (I), trade (F), or museum collections (A), represent secondary contexts or displaced locations.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
