      "generated_answer": "The passage is an excerpt from the Truman Doctrine speech delivered to Congress on March 12, 1947. In this speech, President Truman requested $400 million in emergency economic and military aid to support Greece and Turkey to prevent them from falling under Soviet influence. This policy established the foundation for the U.S. strategy of containment during the Cold War.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
