      "generated_answer": "Aurignacian technology, associated with Upper Paleolithic modern humans, represented a significant shift toward the production of long, thin blades from prepared cores. This method was much more efficient than the Mousterian flake-based technology used by Neanderthals, resulting in a greater length of usable cutting edge per unit of raw stone. Therefore, the most defining difference in the provided options is the increased efficiency in blade production.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
