    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Carlsbad Resolutions were a series of reactionary restrictions introduced by Klemens von Metternich to maintain the conservative order established at the Congress of Vienna. By mandating censorship and monitoring universities, Metternich aimed to stifle the growing liberal and nationalist movements that threatened the stability of the multi-ethnic Austrian Empire and the German Confederation. Therefore, the resolutions were designed to prevent the spread of revolutionary ideals and maintain monarchical control.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
