      "generated_answer": "The poem describes \"District Officers\" demanding land taxes even when the men are away at war and the fields are overgrown with brambles, indicating a persistent administrative presence. This reflects the Tang Dynasty's ability to maintain a functioning, albeit burdensome, administrative apparatus to collect revenue and manage local affairs during times of conflict.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
