      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **E**. Archaeological evidence for trade between these civilizations primarily consists of Harappan stamp seals found in Mesopotamian cities (like Ur and Kish) and Mesopotamian cylinder seals found in Indus Valley sites. While cuneiform tablets mention a land called \"Meluhja\" (believed to be the Indus region), the physical presence of these distinct seals in both regions provides the most direct evidence of commercial exchange.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
