    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D**.\n\nArticle 1 of Source 1 expresses the expectation that Venezuela and New Granada would remain united in a single, powerful republic (Gran Colombia). This expectation was undermined by **sectionalism**, as regional elites in Venezuela, Ecuador, and New Granada prioritized their own local political and economic interests, leading to the eventual dissolution of the union into separate nations by 1831.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
