      "generated_answer": "The statement by Woodrow Wilson emphasizes the duty of \"impartial neutrality\" and avoiding involvement in foreign conflicts, which aligns with the traditional American foreign policy of non-entanglement. This sentiment is most in harmony with **Washington's Farewell Address**, in which George Washington famously warned the United States to avoid permanent alliances and stay out of European wars. The other options represent speeches focused on domestic issues, civil rights, or active international engagement and intervention.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
