    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4740",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"If it be conceded, as it must be by every one who is the least conversant with our institutions, that the sovereign powers delegated are divided between the General and State Governments, and that the latter hold their portion by the same tenure as the former, it would seem impossible to deny to the States the right of deciding on the infractions of their powers, and the proper remedy to be applied for their correction. The right of judging, in such cases, is an essential attribute of sovereignty, of which the States cannot be divested without losing their sovereignty itself, and being reduced to a subordinate corporate condition. In fact, to divide power, and to give to one of the parties the exclusive right of judging of the portion allotted to each, is, in reality, not to divide it at all; and to reserve such exclusive right to the General Government (it matters not by what department to be exercised), is to convert it, in fact, into a great consolidated government, with unlimited powers, and to divest the States, in reality, of all their rights, It is impossible to understand the force of terms, and to deny so plain a conclusion.\"\n—John C. Calhoun, \"South Carolina Exposition and Protest,\" 1828\nThe issue that precipitated the passage excerpted above was\n\nOptions: \nA. the question of secession from the Union.\nB. the enactment of the Missouri Compromise.\nC. the issue of slavery in new territories.\nD. the purchase of Louisiana territory.\nE. the removal of American Indians from the South.\nF. the passage of an act creating higher tariff rates.\nG. the debate over states' rights.\nH. the funding of \"internal improvements.\"\nI. the rechartering of the Second Bank of the United States.\nJ. the passing of the Fugitive Slave Act.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The provided text is from John C. Calhoun's \"South Carolina Exposition and Protest,\" which was written in response to the \"Tariff of Abominations\" (the Tariff of 1828). While the text argues broadly about states' rights and nullification, the specific historical event that precipitated this document was the passage of high protective tariffs that disproportionately harmed the Southern economy. Therefore, the correct option is the act creating higher tariff rates.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
