      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **H**.\n\nThe Counterculture Movement of the 1960s was primarily defined by its opposition to the Vietnam War (as highlighted in the provided text by John Kerry) and its support for the Civil Rights Movement, both of which challenged established social and political norms. While other issues like environmentalism and women's rights gained traction during this era, the anti-war sentiment and the struggle for racial equality were the two most central and mobilizing political pillars of the movement.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
