    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In the provided text, Beveridge argues that the United States has a \"duty to the world\" and a \"mission\" to provide \"civilizing government\" to people he deems incapable of self-rule. He justifies imperialism by claiming it rescues these populations from \"savage\" rule and protects them from other global powers. Therefore, his argument is rooted in the idea of a moral obligation to govern less developed nations.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
