      "generated_answer": "Based on the text of the poem, Kipling portrays imperialism as a strenuous duty (\"heavy harness\") that requires sacrifice (\"bind your sons to exile\") for the benefit of others, despite the lack of gratitude or success. While he uses derogatory language to describe the subjects, he frames the endeavor as a moral obligation that must be accepted. Therefore, the most encompassing summary of this specific conception is that it is a difficult but necessary task.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
