    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4811",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"Wherever I go—the street, the shop, the house, or the steamboat—I hear the people talk in such a way as to indicate that they are yet unable to conceive of the Negro as possessing any rights at all. Men who are honorable in their dealings with their white neighbors will cheat a Negro without feeling a single twinge of their honor. To kill a Negro they do not deem murder; to debauch a Negro woman they do not think fornication; to take the property away from a Negro they do not consider robbery. The people boast that when they get freedmen affairs in their own hands, to use their own classic expression, 'the niggers will catch hell.'\n\"The reason of all this is simple and manifest. The whites esteem the blacks their property by natural right, and however much they may admit that the individual relations of masters and slaves have been destroyed by the war and the President's emancipation proclamation, they still have an ingrained feeling that the blacks at large belong to the whites at large, and whenever opportunity serves they treat the colored people just as their profit, caprice or passion may dictate.\"\n—Congressional testimony of Col. Samuel Thomas, Assistant Commissioner, Bureau of Refugees, Freedmen and Abandoned Lands, 1865\nWhich of the following factors did Alexander Hamilton believe was a source for the problems in the excerpt from Federalist #15?\n\nOptions: \nA. economic class divisions among the American people that prevented them from forging a unified vision.\nB. a failure of American policy-makers to abandon mercantilist principles and to embrace a laissez-faire approach to trade.\nC. The absence of a proper legal system to enforce the law.\nD. The lack of economic development and industrialization.\nE. A lack of proper education among the American people.\nF. The lack of a strong military force to maintain peace and order.\nG. The persistence of slavery and racial discrimination.\nH. a weak central government without the powers to address pressing issues.\nI. The absence of a unified national identity among the American people.\nJ. an unhealthy obsession among the American people with religion and individual salvation, at the expense of interest in solving practical national problems.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **H**.\n\nIn *Federalist #15*, Alexander Hamilton argues that the primary source of the young nation's problems was the \"imbecility\" of the Articles of Confederation, which created a weak central government incapable of enforcing laws or addressing national crises. While the provided excerpt by Col. Samuel Thomas describes the social and racial failures of the Reconstruction era, Hamilton’s specific argument in the context of the Federalist Papers focuses on the structural failure of a government that lacks the power to regulate the conduct of its citizens or states. Therefore, the \"source for the problems\" in Hamilton's view was the lack of a strong, centralized federal authority.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
