      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A**.\n\nIn the excerpt, Thomas Paine emphasizes that \"My own mind is my own church\" and argues that national religious institutions are \"human inventions\" used to \"monopolize power and profit.\" This reflects the Enlightenment characteristic of prioritizing individual reason and personal belief systems over the dogma and authority of organized, state-sponsored religions.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
