      "generated_answer": "During the era of the Qing Dynasty (specifically under the Canton System), the Chinese government restricted maritime trade by confining Western merchants to specific ports, most notably Canton (Guangzhou). This system allowed the empire to control foreign influence and regulate commerce through licensed Chinese merchants known as the Cohong. The other options are historically inaccurate, as trade did occur but was strictly geographically limited.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{H}.",
